…¤book§chapter$«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkWhen Michaiah the son of Gemariah, the son of Shaphan, had heard out of the book all the words of the LORD,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚthen he went down into the king's house, into the scribe's chamber: and, lo, all the princes sat there, even Elishama the scribe, and Delaiah the son of Shemaiah, and Elnathan the son of Achbor, and Gemariah the son of Shaphan, and Zedekiah the son of Hananiah, and all the princes.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvThen Michaiah declared unto them all the words that he had heard, when Baruch read the book in the ears of the people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚTherefore all the princes sent Jehudi the son of Nethaniah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Cushi, unto Baruch, saying, Take in thine hand the roll wherein thou hast read in the ears of the people, and come. So Baruch the son of Neriah took the roll in his hand, and came unto them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And they said unto him, Sit down now, and read it in our ears. So Baruch read it in their ears.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter$«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£Now it came to pass, when they had heard all the words, they were afraid both one and other, and said unto Baruch, We will surely tell the king of all these words.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And they asked Baruch, saying, Tell us now, how didst thou write all these words at his mouth?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwThen Baruch answered them, He pronounced all these words unto me with his mouth, and I wrote them with ink in the book.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeThen said the princes unto Baruch, Go, hide thee, thou and Jeremiah; and let no man know where ye be.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter$«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd they went in to the king into the court, but they laid up the roll in the chamber of Elishama the scribe, and told all the words in the ears of the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËSo the king sent Jehudi to fetch the roll: and he took it out of Elishama the scribe's chamber. And Jehudi read it in the ears of the king, and in the ears of all the princes which stood beside the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnNow the king sat in the winterhouse in the ninth month: and there was a fire on the hearth burning before him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ×And it came to pass, that when Jehudi had read three or four leaves, he cut it with the penknife, and cast it into the fire that was on the hearth, until all the roll was consumed in the fire that was on the hearth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxYet they were not afraid, nor rent their garments, neither the king, nor any of his servants that heard all these words.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNevertheless Elnathan and Delaiah and Gemariah had made intercession to the king that he would not burn the roll: but he would not hear them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁBut the king commanded Jerahmeel the son of Hammelech, and Seraiah the son of Azriel, and Shelemiah the son of Abdeel, to take Baruch the scribe and Jeremiah the prophet: but the LORD hid them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter$«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah, after that the king had burned the roll, and the words which Baruch wrote at the mouth of Jeremiah, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTake thee again another roll, and write in it all the former words that were in the first roll, which Jehoiakim the king of Judah hath burned.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd thou shalt say to Jehoiakim king of Judah, Thus saith the LORD; Thou hast burned this roll, saying, Why hast thou written therein, saying, The king of Babylon shall certainly come and destroy this land, and shall cause to cease from thence man and beast?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÈTherefore thus saith the LORD of Jehoiakim king of Judah; He shall have none to sit upon the throne of David: and his dead body shall be cast out in the day to the heat, and in the night to the frost.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙïAnd I will punish him and his seed and his servants for their iniquity; and I will bring upon them, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and upon the men of Judah, all the evil that I have pronounced against them; but they hearkened not.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter$«first_verse ªlast_verse ¦verses‘„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ
Then took Jeremiah another roll, and gave it to Baruch the scribe, the son of Neriah; who wrote therein from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words of the book which Jehoiakim king of Judah had burned in the fire: and there were added besides unto them many like words.¦layout ªlast_verse 